new file mode 100644
index 0000000..86654b8
--- /dev/null
+++ b/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,45 @@
+# Users API
+
+Functions in `src/api/`. Every function takes the database as its first argument and throws an `Error` (`<name>: db is required`) if `db` is `undefined` or `null`.
+
+A **User** is `{ id, email, fullName, createdAt, lastLogin, nickname }`. `createdAt` and `lastLogin` are ISO timestamps, `lastLogin` is `null` until a login is recorded, and `nickname` is `null` when the user has none.
+
+## `src/api/users.js`
+
+| Function | Description |
+| --- | --- |
+| `createUser(db, { email, fullName, nickname })` | Creates a user with a generated id and creation time and returns it. `nickname` is optional (`null` counts as not set); like `fullName` it must be 1-100 characters when given. Throws if `fullName` is not 1-100 characters, `email` has no `"@"`, or the email is already taken (case-insensitive). |
+| `getUser(db, id)` | Returns the user with that id, or `null`. |
+| `getUserByEmail(db, email)` | Returns the user with that email, ignoring case, or `null`. Also `null` if `email` is not a string. |
+| `listUsers(db, { limit, offset })` | Returns users oldest first. `limit` defaults to no limit and `offset` to 0. Throws if either is negative or not an integer. |
+| `countUsers(db)` | Returns the number of users. |
+| `recordLogin(db, id, when)` | Sets the user's `lastLogin` (`when` defaults to now; a `Date`, timestamp or date string) and returns the updated user, or `null` if there is no such user. |
+| `updateUser(db, id, { email, fullName })` | Changes only the fields given and returns the updated user, or `null` if there is no such user. Applies the same checks as `createUser`; a user may change the case of their own email. Nothing is changed if a check fails. |
+| `deleteUser(db, id)` | Removes the user. Returns `true`, or `false` if there was no such user. |
+| `searchUsers(db, query)` | Returns users whose `fullName` or `email` contains `query`, ignoring case, oldest first. Returns `[]` if `query` is not a string. |
+
+```js
+const { createUser, listUsers } = require('./src/api/users.js');
+
+const ada = createUser(db, { email: 'ada@example.com', fullName: 'Ada Lovelace' });
+listUsers(db, { limit: 10, offset: 0 }); // [ada]
+```
+
+## `src/api/export.js`
+
+| Function | Description |
+| --- | --- |
+| `exportUsersCsv(db)` | Returns all users as CSV: a header row `id,email,fullName,createdAt,lastLogin`, then one row per user, oldest first. Fields containing commas, quotes or newlines are quoted. Rows end with `\n`. |
+| `importUsersCsv(db, csv)` | The inverse of `exportUsersCsv`. Keeps ids and timestamps and returns the number of users imported. Every row is checked first, so an invalid file (wrong header or field count, bad email, name or date, duplicate id or email) throws and imports nothing. |
+
+## `src/api/format.js`
+
+| Function | Description |
+| --- | --- |
+| `displayName(user)` | Returns `user.fullName`, or the part of the email before `"@"` when `fullName` is empty or blank. |
+
+## Tests
+
+```
+npm test
+```
