+
+/**
+ * The p-th percentile of an array of numbers, by linear interpolation between the closest ranks (the
+ * "inclusive" method of Excel's PERCENTILE.INC and NumPy's default): percentile(xs, 0) is the smallest
+ * item, percentile(xs, 100) the largest and percentile(xs, 50) the median. For example
+ * percentile([1, 2, 3, 4, 5], 25) is 2 and percentile([1, 2, 3, 4], 90) is 3.7. An empty array gives NaN,
+ * and so does any NaN in the input. Infinities sort as expected; an interpolation between -Infinity and
+ * +Infinity is NaN. Huge finite numbers do not overflow. The input is not modified.
+ * @param {number[]} xs
+ * @param {number} p from 0 to 100, both included; may be fractional
+ * @returns {number}
+ * @throws {TypeError} if xs is not an array, has an item that is not a number (a hole counts as undefined),
+ *   or p is not a number
+ * @throws {RangeError} if p is NaN or outside 0..100
